# ARCHER — Update Instructions for Antigravity (v2)

**This document supersedes `ARCHER_ANTIGRAVITY_UPDATE_INSTRUCTIONS.md`.** Everything in v1 is either carried forward below (with several of its open decisions now resolved) or superseded by the single-agent architecture work in Section 6. Read this one; treat v1 as historical.

**Source:** Live review of `JaxArcher/ARCHER_9` (`pyproject.toml`, `config.py`, `orchestrator.py`, `voice/tts.py`, `voice/wake_word.py`, `observer/*`, `agents/inventory_agent.py`, `agents/blindspot_agent.py`, `docker-compose.yml`), plus design discussion covering conversation architecture, memory, and agent structure.

**How to use this doc:** No timelines by design. Sections 1-5 are direct fixes and cleanup to the *existing* system — do these regardless of the bigger architecture work. Section 6 is new construction: a single-agent core built alongside the current system, not a replacement for it yet. Do the Phase 0 audit described at the end of v1 before starting either — confirm this doc still matches `master` before acting on it.

