## 5. Observer — move the vision model off GPU VRAM

**Files:** `observer/analyzers.py` (`SceneAnalyzer`), `config.py`
`SceneAnalyzer` currently sends `qwen2.5vl:7b` requests to `self._config.ollama_base_url` — the *same* GPU-bound Ollama instance used for conversation and local fallback. This was originally speced to run separately on CPU/system RAM (256GB available), which never made it into the current code.

Observer only analyzes a frame every 30 seconds (`observer_analysis_frequency`, `SceneAnalyzer`'s own cooldown) — nowhere near latency-sensitive, so CPU inference taking 10-15 seconds per call is fine. Run a second Ollama instance bound to CPU only (`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=""`, separate port, e.g. 11435), add a new config field (e.g. `observer_ollama_url`) distinct from `ollama_base_url`, and point `SceneAnalyzer` at it. This frees several GB of VRAM on the RTX 5080 for whichever model comes out of Section 6.5.

