## Ground rules (unchanged from v1)

- No timelines or target dates in any documentation.
- Don't add CPU-fallback code paths silently — if a local model or service doesn't have GPU available where it's supposed to, fail loudly rather than degrading quietly. (Section 5's Observer CPU move is an intentional, explicit exception — that one's designed to run on CPU, not falling back to it.)
- `pyttsx3` remains permanently forbidden.
- Do the Phase 0 audit before starting — confirm this doc still matches `master`, report anything that's already fixed or already stale rather than silently skipping it.
- Git-sourced skills/tools (e.g. OfficeCLI) are intentionally out of scope for this round — separate, unresolved discussion.